# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-efile-write-not-applied-to-l-file — -Efile-write never reaches the OPEN calls of the -l file (or -x forms) on the CAD backends, silently
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: CAD run (encoding:experiment:lispsys-bom:autocad:windows, encoding:experiment:bricscad:windows)
#+BRANCH: alfe-efile-write-all-actions
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Context

Found 2026-10-08 reading the end-to-end check of the AutoCAD -Efile-write
forwarding (=encoding-situations-cli-options=, measurement 3). alfe forwards
-Efile-write to the CAD's own OPEN by rewriting OPEN calls into the bootstrap's
=alfe-open*= (",ccs=" on BricsCAD/Windows, the third argument "utf8" on
AutoCAD at LISPSYS 1/2). The rewrite is done by =alfe-load= only
(=*alfe-load-rewrite*= set, =alfe-eval-rewritten-form=).

* Problem

=alfe --autocad -Efile-write utf-8 -l prog.lsp= does not forward anything to
the OPEN calls in =prog.lsp=, and says nothing. The =-l= action is sent as a
=(load "<staged path>")= request (=backend-cad-common.lisp=, the =:load=
branch); the CAD side evaluates it through =autolisp-eval-request-form= ->
=autolisp-eval-load-form= -> =autolisp-source-load=, with
=*alfe-load-rewrite*= NIL, so each form goes through
=autolisp-eval-request-form=, which never rewrites OPEN. The same holds for
=-x= forms and for a nested native =(load ...)= in such a file.

Evidence: job 16998925786 (encoding:experiment:lispsys-bom:autocad:windows,
pipeline 2922145991, AutoCAD 2022): =lispsys-forward-probe.lsp=, loaded with
=-l= under =-Efile-write utf-8=, printed =FORWARDED-ARG "utf8"= (the variable
was set) but =w SIZE 3= and =a SIZE 1= at LISPSYS 0, 1 and 2, and no WARN line
at any level -- =alfe-open*= was never called (it warns unconditionally at
LISPSYS 0).

The user manual says the forwarding applies "in code loaded with =alfe-load="
and that the native =load= and =-x= forms are left alone, but it never said
the =-l= file itself is not loaded with =alfe-load= (2026-10-08: now it does,
with the workaround: give =-l= a file that =alfe-load=-s the program).

* Proposal

Either (pjb):
1. rewrite OPEN (only OPEN, only while =alfe-open-rewrite-p=) in the request
   path too, so the =-l= file and =-x= forms are covered; the cons-identity
   guard (=alfe-form-needs-rewrite-p=) already limits rebuilding to forms that
   contain an OPEN call when forwarding is active. Needs a CAD run (AutoCAD and
   BricsCAD/Windows) before it ships, since the request path's eval was the
   one that broke on rebuilt conses ("division par zero") before the guard; or
2. keep it as is (documented now) and warn once when -Efile-write is
   forwarded but the run's =-l= file contains a literal OPEN call.

* Acceptance criteria

- =alfe --autocad -Efile-write utf-8 -l f.lsp= with =(open p "w")= in =f.lsp=
  writes UTF-8 at LISPSYS 1/2 (option 1), or warns (option 2);
- a unit test with the hosted clautolisp engine (as
  =protocol-alfe-load-forwards-open-write-arg=) through the =:load= action.

* Decision (pjb, 2026-10-08)

"yes, apply -Efile-write to -l and -x too." -- option 1.

* Resolution (clautolisp 2.3.14 / alfe 2.3.14, branch alfe-efile-write-all-actions)

Implemented; stays NEXT until the CAD runs below verify it.

** Where OPEN is rewritten, per action path

Every action other than alfe-load reaches the CAD as a protocol request
evaluated by =autolisp-eval-request-source=: =-l= (sent as
=(load "<staged>")=, then each form of the file through the deported loader's
read loop, =autolisp-source-load-run-body-impl=), =-x=, =--main= (=(main)=),
REPL input (=(print TEXT)=), the batch request loops (=autolisp-run-eval-file=,
the REPL file loop) and any other request. That function is the one place
changed:

- run-common.lsp's override (file-protocol.lisp): =alfe-request-source-text=
  first asks =alfe-open-request-p= (-Efile-write forwarded, i.e.
  =*ALFE-OPEN-WRITE-CCS*= or =*ALFE-OPEN-WRITE-ARG*= set, AND the form calls
  OPEN outside QUOTE / FUNCTION); if so, the text written to alfe-eval.lsp is
  =alfe-open-request-text='s;
- the bootstrap's default =autolisp-eval-request-form= (direct eval, used
  only without run-common's override) evaluates
  =(alfe-rewrite-open-calls form)= under the same test;
- alfe-load is unchanged (it already rewrote OPEN along with the rest).

** Why a TEXT rewrite: the source is not re-printed

Two other ways were rejected:
1. evaluating in an environment where OPEN is alfe-open*: AutoCAD's DEFUN has
   no &rest and OPEN takes 2 or 3 arguments, so no shadow can stand in for it
   there (the very reason alfe-load rewrites calls instead of shadowing);
2. the form walk alone, as alfe-load does: the request path hands TEXT to the
   CAD's LOAD, so the rebuilt form would have to be printed back -- what
   MR !466 (alfe-cad-transport-rounds-reals) removed.

So =alfe-open-rewrite-text= (bootstrap) rewrites the source text itself:
"(open ARGS)" becomes "(alfe-open* (list ARGS))" and nothing else changes --
real literals keep every digit, comments and spacing stay. It skips strings,
; and ;| |; comments, and lists quoted by ' or headed by QUOTE / FUNCTION:
the textual twin of the OPEN-only form walk =alfe-rewrite-open-calls=. As a
guard, the rewritten text is READ back and used only if it is EQUAL to the
walk's result; otherwise -- and when there is no text, or when the AutoCAD
princ normaliser already rebuilt the form (which is then printed anyway) --
the walked form is printed with autolisp-form-source-text (lossless reals).
Either way the CAD's LOAD reads fresh text, so no rebuilt cons is evaluated
on the CAD (the "division par zero" concern above). Without -Efile-write none
of this runs and no request changes.

The measured semantics stay alfe-open*'s: AutoCAD "w"/"a" get "utf8" at
LISPSYS 1/2, at LISPSYS 0 nothing is forwarded and ONE warning is given per
run; BricsCAD/Windows ",ccs=UTF-8"/UTF-16LE on "w"/"a"; macOS BricsCAD
nothing.

Not reached (documented in the alfe manual): an OPEN that exists only at run
time -- =(apply 'open ...)=, a quoted =(open ...)= evaluated later, a file
read by a native LOAD nested inside an expression (a top-level =(load ...)=
request goes through the deported loader and IS covered).

** Tests (autolisp-front-end/tests/file-protocol-tests.lisp, hosted clautolisp)

- protocol-open-write-arg-reaches-every-action: AutoCAD-style runtime
  (fixed-arity shadows; dialect autocad-2022, whose default write is
  cp1252), *ALFE-OPEN-WRITE-ARG* "utf8": the -l file's "w" and "a", --main,
  -x and a REPL request all write UTF-8 at LISPSYS 1/2 (alfe-open* called 5
  times, no warning); at LISPSYS 0 they write the default with exactly one
  warning for the run; a quoted OPEN stays data; real literals exact; the -l
  file is not re-printed.
- protocol-open-write-ccs-reaches-every-action: BricsCAD-style (variadic),
  *ALFE-OPEN-WRITE-CCS* "UTF-16LE": the same five, in UTF-16LE.
- protocol-open-not-rewritten-without-efile-write: both runtimes without
  -Efile-write: every file as the unrewritten reference, alfe-open* never
  called, nothing re-printed.
- protocol-open-rewrite-text-keeps-the-source: the text rewriter, 7 cases.
- protocol-lispsys-forward-probe-three-ways: the CAD probe run the three ways
  the CI script runs it, against the expectations the job is read with.
Seen red: with alfe-open-request-p forced to NIL, 16 checks fail.

** CAD verification -- NOT yet run (keep NEXT)

- encoding:experiment:lispsys-bom:autocad:windows (run-lispsys-bom-probe.ps1)
  runs lispsys-forward-probe.lsp three ways per LISPSYS level, report tags
  =[LISPSYS n forward alfe-load]=, =[LISPSYS n forward -l]=,
  =[LISPSYS n forward -x]=. Expected for EACH: LISPSYS 0 -> w SIZE 3,
  a SIZE 1, one WARN; LISPSYS 1/2 -> w SIZE 4, a SIZE 2, no WARN.
- encoding:experiment:bricscad:windows (run-encoding-experiment.ps1) has a
  new FORWARD step, the same three ways: expected w SIZE 7 (BOM + UTF-8),
  a SIZE 2 or 5 (fresh-file "a,ccs=UTF-8", not measured), no WARN; 3 / 1
  would mean not forwarded. encoding:experiment:autocad:windows runs the same
  step at the runner's own LISPSYS.
Close (DONE, issues/closed/, TRIAGE row DONE) once those read as expected.

** Reconciliation with MR !464

This branch carries !464's three encoding commits cherry-picked unchanged
(44763bb7, 1b5e1fe4, 18eb62a8: the "a" "utf8" forwarding, this ticket, the
BricsCAD append measurement), because the measured "a" semantics and the
probe's alfe-load entry pass are prerequisites. The "-l limitation /
workaround" text !464 added (alfe user manual, alfe spec, RELEASE_NOTES,
backend-cad-common.lisp comment, run-lispsys-bom-probe.ps1 and
lispsys-forward-probe.lsp headers) is REPLACED on this branch: when the
stacks are reconciled, keep this branch's wording (the cherry-picks merge as
identical changes).
